<title>UK: APV jumps after possible bid approach.</title>
<headline>APV jumps after possible bid approach.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares APV Plc advanced 15-1/2p or 22 percent to 86-1/2 on Wednesday, after news that the engineering and components group had received an &quot;indication of interest&quot; that may result in a bid being made for the company, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;We are seeing trade in the stock but nobody knows if a deal will go through,&quot; said one dealer.</p>
<p>In a short statement made as the market closed on Tuesday, the company said it was not clear whether &quot;the approach will or will not lead to an offer being made for APV.&quot;</p>
<p>The Board of APV said it would keep shareholders informed of developments.</p>
<p>-- Andrew Langlands, London Newsroom +44 171 542 3496</p>
